<div id="2026-11-12-schema-compare-result-display" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-12 — Schema-compare: show Result-file settings (Extra, Comment, Size, Nullable)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The schema-compare field grid and the tables list left the Result-file side looking empty. <code>schema_compare_table</code> hard-coded Result <code>extra</code> and <code>comment</code> to an empty string; Template Toolkit cannot print ARRAY/HASH refs, so <code>size =&gt; [10, 2]</code> and <code>extra =&gt; { list =&gt; [...] }</code> rendered as blank cells; undeclared <code>is_nullable</code> printed as a blank Nullable cell; and the tables list only parsed Result columns for orphan (result-only) files, so matched tables showed a filename and no Result settings.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> <code>ResultParser::format_column_for_display</code> and <code>preview_fields</code> flatten those attributes to printable scalars (size <code>(10,2)</code>, enum extra, <code>auto_increment</code>, comment/docs, nullable YES/NO/—). <code>schema_compare_table</code> uses that for Result rows. <code>schema_compare_database</code> attaches the same preview to matched tables; <code>tables.tt</code> shows a collapsed “Result file settings” grid. Verified with <code>t/schema_compare_result_display.t</code> (and existing parser/equivalence tests).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Schema/ResultParser.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/SchemaComparison.pm</code>, <code>root/admin/schema_compare/tables.tt</code>, <code>root/admin/schema_compare/fields.tt</code>, <code>t/schema_compare_result_display.t</code>, this changelog fragment.</p>
</div>
